-- title:
--   No monic value p(j) in mathfrak m_V at a non-maximal centre
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative local ring, $F$ a field equipped with an $R$-algebra structure, and $j \in F$. Write $C =$ `chartAlgFin R F j` for the $R$-subalgebra of $F$ consisting of the elements of $F$ that are integral over the $R$-subalgebra generated by $j$. Let $V \subseteq F$ be a valuation subring such that: the image of every $a \in R$ under the structure map $R \to F$ lies in $V$; for every $a$ in the maximal ideal of $R$ the corresponding element of $V$ lies in the maximal ideal of $V$; and every element of $C$ lies in $V$. Let $y$ be an ideal of $C$ characterised by the condition that an element $c \in C$ belongs to $y$ precisely when, viewed as an element of $V$, it lies in the maximal ideal of $V$ — that is, $y$ is the centre $\mathfrak m_V \cap C$ of $V$ on $C$. Assume $y$ is not a maximal ideal of $C$. Then, assuming $j \in V$, for every monic polynomial $p \in R[X]$ the element $p(j) \in F$, obtained by evaluating the image of $p$ in $F[X]$ at $j$ and regarded as an element of $V$, does not lie in the maximal ideal of $V$.
--
--   This is the statement that a valuation of $F$ whose centre on the $j$-finite chart algebra is a non-maximal prime is of Igusa type: the residue of $j$ is transcendental over the residue field of $R$, since no monic integral relation over $R$ can be satisfied by $j$ modulo $\mathfrak m_V$. It is used in the analysis of the valuations of the function field of the full-level modular curve occurring along Igusa branches of the special fibre, in particular by the results on Igusa-type valuation subrings and on units outside the maximal ideal at exceptional Igusa points.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel_forall_monic_aeval_not_mem_maximalIdeal_of_not_isMaximal_centre.lean

